 "result_text": "I changed `aws_google_auth/__init__.py` so that credentials are no longer written to the AWS files when no profile is set. I didn't run the tool or the tests.\n\nThe `[None]` section came from `main()`. It printed the export commands when `config.profile` was `None`, then called `_store(config, token)` anyway. `_store` wrote a section literally named `None` into `~/.aws/credentials`, plus a `profile None` section into `~/.aws/config`.\n\nNow, with no profile, the tool only prints the exports. With a profile, it stores credentials as before.\n\nI didn't trace how two runs turn those writes into the `DuplicateSectionError`. Removing the `None` writes should stop new bad sections from appearing. Any existing `[None]` sections in your `~/.aws/credentials` will need to be deleted by hand.",
